these are the 5 key insights the project is designed to uncover:

House prices are likely positively skewed
The notebook calculates the skewness of the Price column.
Real-estate datasets typically contain a few extremely expensive properties, causing the average price to be higher than the median price.
Larger houses tend to have higher prices
The correlation between Area of the house (excluding basement) and Price is analyzed.
A positive correlation would indicate that living area is one of the strongest predictors of house value.
More bedrooms generally increase property value
The project finds the most common number of bedrooms and calculates average price by bedroom count.
Houses with more bedrooms usually command higher prices because they offer greater living capacity.
Premium features significantly affect price
The notebook compares average prices based on:
Number of floors
Waterfront presence
Waterfront properties and larger multi-floor homes typically have substantially higher average prices than standard properties.
Location is a major determinant of house prices
The analysis identifies postal codes with the highest average house prices.
This highlights how neighborhood desirability, infrastructure, and accessibility influence real-estate values.
